{"success": true, "message": "Test details sent successfully", "data": {"test": {"_id": "69de21f17e39d99b57bc5b11", "analysisVideoCdn": "yt", "exam": ["605dfcb2f226ac25a8bd5fef"], "ctype": null, "position": 0, "order": 12, "enableCalculator": false, "isContinuousQuestion": false, "reattemptAvailable": false, "singleSectionMultipleSubjects": false, "timeRestricted": false, "title": "Atomic Physics - Test 1", "description": "Previous Year Questions as Chapter Test", "syllabus": "This test contains questions from all topics of this chapter included in the JEE Main syllabus. It includes a mix of questions from PYQs of JEE Main 2019 - 2025.", "totalTime": 50, "totalQuestions": 25, "totalMarks": 100, "bonusQuestions": null, "bonusMarks": null, "startDate": "2026-04-15T03:30:00.000Z", "endDate": "2027-04-30T00:00:00.000Z", "type": "free", "class": "605df635a37b7025c438d685", "instruction": "608289ffb160b022e9442c83", "subjects": [{"subjectId": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "totalMarks": 100, "bonusMarks": 0, "totalQuestions": 25, "bonusQuestions": 0, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e458"}], "sections": [{"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e413", "title": "Physics Single Correct", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3aa", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ac"], "topics": ["6117b8be67dbe2603c3e8673"], "concepts": ["6117b8bd67dbe2603c3e8594"], "question": {"text": "The recoil speed of a hydrogen atom after it emits a photon in going from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math>&nbsp;state to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math>&nbsp;state will be"}, "options": [{"id": "9d6cd3", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>17</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3ab"}, {"id": "1c781a", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>19</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3ac"}, {"id": "10b847", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>34</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3ad"}, {"id": "5b8c56", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3ae"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3af", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ac"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4766"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b2d"], "question": {"text": "A hydrogen atom, initially in the ground state is excited by absorbing a photon of wavelength $980 Ã…$. The radius of the atom in the excited state, in terms of Bohr radius $a_{0}$, will be:"}, "options": [{"id": "1933d8", "text": "$25 \\mathrm{a}_{0}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3b0"}, {"id": "302f68", "text": "$9 a_{0}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3b1"}, {"id": "18a864", "text": "$16 \\mathrm{a}_{0}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3b2"}, {"id": "861f06", "text": "None of the above", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3b3"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3b4", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ac"], "topics": ["60e2fb5766f9ce3f243b4f3c"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f03"], "question": {"text": "Arrange the following in the ascending order of wavelength $(\\lambda)$ :\n(A) Microwaves $\\left(\\lambda_1\\right)$\n(B) Ultraviolet rays $\\left(\\lambda_2\\right)$\n(C) Infrared rays $\\left(\\lambda_3\\right)$\n(D) X-rays $\\left(\\lambda_4\\right)$\n\nChoose the most appropriate answer from the options given below :"}, "options": [{"id": "85a1b8", "text": "$\\lambda_4 \\lt \\lambda_3 \\lt \\lambda_2 \\lt \\lambda_1$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3b5"}, {"id": "ca739d", "text": "$\\lambda_3 \\lt \\lambda_4 \\lt \\lambda_2 \\lt \\lambda_1$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3b6"}, {"id": "4b1301", "text": "$\\lambda_4 \\lt \\lambda_3 \\lt \\lambda_1 \\lt \\lambda_2$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3b7"}, {"id": "d43cc9", "text": "$\\lambda_4 \\lt \\lambda_2 \\lt \\lambda_3 \\lt \\lambda_1$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3b8"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3b9", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ac"], "topics": ["6162fb5a6ed13040ec84de88"], "concepts": ["6162fb5a6ed13040ec84de5f"], "question": {"text": "Given below are two statements:<br/>Statement I: Most of the mass of the atom and all its positive charge are concentrated in a tiny nucleus and the electrons revolve around it, is Rutherford's model.<br/>Statement II: An atom is a spherical cloud of positive charges with electrons embedded in it, is a special case of Rutherford's model.<br/>In the light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate from the options given below."}, "options": [{"id": "d7c944", "text": "Both statement I and statement II are false", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3ba"}, {"id": "441de0", "text": "Statement I is false but statement II is true", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3bb"}, {"id": "cee3ee", "text": "Statement I is true but statement II is false", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3bc"}, {"id": "4d21d1", "text": "Both statement I and statement II are true", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3bd"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3be", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ac"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4766"], "concepts": ["6117b98967dbe2603c3ea31d"], "question": {"text": "The angular momentum for the electron in Bohr&rsquo;s orbit is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi></math>. If the electron is assumed to revolve in second orbit of hydrogen atom, then the change in angular momentum will be"}, "options": [{"id": "ad8206", "text": "Zero", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3bf"}, {"id": "e72c16", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>L</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3c0"}, {"id": "569849", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3c1"}, {"id": "fc7331", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3c2"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3c3", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ac"], "topics": ["60e2fb5766f9ce3f243b4f3c"], "concepts": ["6117b5e3478ae845c43c5de3"], "question": {"text": "<p>Hydrogen atom from excited state comes to the ground by emitting a photon of wavelength <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#955;</mi></math>. The value of principal quantum number <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math>&nbsp;of the excited state will be :</p><p>( <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>:</mo></math> Rydberg constant)</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "c0e2dc", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>R</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3c4"}, {"id": "c91612", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>R</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>R</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3c5"}, {"id": "72cb43", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mfrac><mi>&#955;</mi><mrow><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>R</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3c6"}, {"id": "a488df", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#955;</mi><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>R</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3c7"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3c8", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ac"], "topics": ["6117b8be67dbe2603c3e8673"], "concepts": ["6162fb5a6ed13040ec84de56"], "question": {"text": "The graph which depicts the results of Rutherford gold foil experiment with <math><mi>&#945;</mi></math> -particles is:<br /><math><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>:</mo></math> Scattering angle<br /><math><mi>Y</mi><mo>:</mo></math> Number of scattered <math><mi>&#945;</mi></math> -particles detected<br />(Plots are schematic and not to scale)"}, "options": [{"id": "db395b", "text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F9acf8be2-3912-4102-8235-9c4f20b5e7d8-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 203px; height: 205px;\" />", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3c9"}, {"id": "d954b8", "text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F212ce0d9-0285-456b-9cfb-8c6ccb9afd22-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 203px; height: 205px;\" />", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3ca"}, {"id": "1a5622", "text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F9440266f-0f2e-45f5-904d-8482e8549a29-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 175px; height: 174px;\" />", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3cb"}, {"id": "54b25e", "text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F12447055-b07a-4af2-b33a-e2b149a65b8e-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 175px; height: 174px;\" />", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3cc"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3cd", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ac"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4766"], "concepts": ["60e5671a499d1e49588f87d3"], "question": {"text": "The momentum of an electron revolving in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi><mo>&#160;</mo></mrow></msup></math> orbit is given by : (Symbols have their usual meanings)"}, "options": [{"id": "145003", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mi>h</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3ce"}, {"id": "2654fa", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mi>h</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3cf"}, {"id": "982566", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mi>h</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3d0"}, {"id": "5f0faa", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mi>h</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3d1"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3d2", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ac"], "topics": ["60e2fb5766f9ce3f243b4f3c"], "concepts": ["60e40fd4f1ef260f84ed1e43"], "question": {"text": "If the wavelength of the first member of Lyman series of hydrogen is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>λ</mi></math>. The wavelength of the second member will be"}, "options": [{"id": "81e92b", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>27</mn><mn>32</mn></mfrac><mi>λ</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3d3"}, {"id": "4e8eb2", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>32</mn><mn>27</mn></mfrac><mi>λ</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3d4"}, {"id": "378931", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>27</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mi>λ</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3d5"}, {"id": "100609", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>27</mn></mfrac><mi>λ</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3d6"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3d7", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ac"], "topics": ["6117b8be67dbe2603c3e8673"], "concepts": ["6117b8bd67dbe2603c3e8594"], "question": {"text": "Considering Bohr's atomic model for hydrogen atom :<br/>(A) the energy of H atom in ground state is same as energy of $\\mathrm{He}^{+}$ion in its first excited state.<br/>(B) the energy of H atom in ground state is same as that for $\\mathrm{Li}^{++}$ion in its second excited state.<br/>(C) the energy of H atom in its ground state is same as that of $\\mathrm{He}^{+}$ion for its ground state.<br/>(D) the energy of $\\mathrm{He}^{+}$ion in its first excited state is same as that for $\\mathrm{Li}^{++}$ion in its ground state<br/>Choose the correct answer from the options given below :"}, "options": [{"id": "b96058", "text": "(B), (D) only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3d8"}, {"id": "f5b46a", "text": "(A), (B) only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3d9"}, {"id": "11683f", "text": "(A), (D) only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3da"}, {"id": "ae8675", "text": "(A), (C) only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3db"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3dc", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ac"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4766"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b471c"], "question": {"text": "Imagine that the electron in a hydrogen atom is replaced by a muon <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>&#956;</mi></mfenced><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;The mass of muon particle is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>207</mn></math> times that of an electron and charge is equal to the charge of an electron. The ionization potential of this hydrogen atom will be:-"}, "options": [{"id": "1c82ee", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>13</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>eV</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3dd"}, {"id": "37164a", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2815</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>eV</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3de"}, {"id": "634879", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>331</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>eV</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3df"}, {"id": "d874c6", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>27</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>eV</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3e0"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3e1", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ac"], "topics": ["60e2fb5766f9ce3f243b4f3c"], "concepts": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52c0"], "question": {"text": "<p>The energy levels of an atom is shown is figure.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F45e23909-e828-4c0e-bd86-7d2abbf6c866-9894466.PNG?alt=media\" style=\"width: 307px; height: 225px;\" /></p><p>Which one of these transitions will result in the emission of a photon of wavelength <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>124</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>nm</mi></math>?</p><p>Given (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>62</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#215;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>&#8211;</mo><mn>34</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>)</p><p>&nbsp;</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "7502cf", "text": "B", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3e2"}, {"id": "2ad425", "text": "A", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3e3"}, {"id": "17e6ab", "text": "C", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3e4"}, {"id": "4df03b", "text": "D", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3e5"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3e6", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ac"], "topics": ["6117b8be67dbe2603c3e8673"], "concepts": ["6162fb5a6ed13040ec84de56"], "question": {"text": "<p>Read the following statements:<br />(A) Volume of the nucleus is directly proportional to the mass number.<br />(B) Volume of the nucleus is independent of mass number.<br />(C) Density of the nucleus is directly proportional to the mass number.<br />(D) Density of the nucleus is directly proportional to the cube root of the mass number.<br />(E) Density of the nucleus is independent of the mass number.</p><p>Choose the correct option from the following options.</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "4f39f6", "text": "(A) and (D) only.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3e7"}, {"id": "d804c6", "text": "(A) and (E) only.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3e8"}, {"id": "2c7640", "text": "(B) and (E) only.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3e9"}, {"id": "78e6bb", "text": "(A) and (C) only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3ea"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3eb", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ac"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4766"], "concepts": ["6162fb5b6ed13040ec84df6b"], "question": {"text": "In<math><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>,electron in first Bohr orbit is excited to a level by a radiation of wavelength<math><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#955;</mi></math>.When the ion gets de excited to the ground state in all possible ways (including intermediate emissions), a total of six spectral lines are observed. What is the value of <math><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#955;</mi></math> ?<br /><br>(Given: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6.63</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>34</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>8</mn></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> )"}, "options": [{"id": "ad0367", "text": "<math><mn>10.8</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3ec"}, {"id": "1d1e2b", "text": "<math><mn>9.4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3ed"}, {"id": "bfb3bd", "text": "<math><mn>11.4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3ee"}, {"id": "64ca50", "text": "<math><mn>12.3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3ef"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3f0", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ac"], "topics": ["60e2fb5766f9ce3f243b4f3c"], "concepts": ["6117b5e3478ae845c43c5de3"], "question": {"text": "In a hydrogen atom the electron makes a transition from&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mi>th</mi></msup></math>&nbsp; level to the&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi>th</mi></msup></math> level. If&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>1</mn></math>, the frequency of radiation emitted is proportional to :"}, "options": [{"id": "04e385", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3f1"}, {"id": "91411d", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3f2"}, {"id": "96c316", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3f3"}, {"id": "24fe97", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3f4"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3f5", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ac"], "topics": ["6117b8be67dbe2603c3e8673"], "concepts": ["6117b8bd67dbe2603c3e8594"], "question": {"text": "Given below are two statements: one is labelled as <strong>Assertion A</strong> and the other is labelled as<br><strong>Reason R</strong>.<br/><strong>Assertion A:</strong> The Bohr model is applicable to hydrogen and hydrogen-like atoms only.<br><strong>Reason R :</strong> The formulation of Bohr model does not include repulsive force between electrons.<br/>In the light of the above statements, choose the<strong> <i>correct</i></strong> answer from the options given below :"}, "options": [{"id": "acad9f", "text": "Both $\\mathrm{A}$ and $\\mathrm{R}$ are true but $\\mathrm{R}$ is NOT the correct explanation of $\\mathrm{A}$.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3f6"}, {"id": "42fceb", "text": "$\\mathrm{A}$ is false but $\\mathrm{R}$ is true.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3f7"}, {"id": "fab820", "text": "Both $\\mathrm{A}$ and $\\mathrm{R}$ are true and $\\mathrm{R}$ is the correct explanation of $\\mathrm{A}$.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3f8"}, {"id": "54cb7e", "text": "$\\mathrm{A}$ is true but $\\mathrm{R}$ is false.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3f9"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3fa", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ac"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4766"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b2d"], "question": {"text": "The radius of electron&#39;s second stationary orbit in Bohr&#39;s atom is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>. The radius of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>3</mn><mrow><mi>r</mi><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></math> orbit will be"}, "options": [{"id": "aa942a", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>R</mi><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3fb"}, {"id": "0014e3", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>R</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3fc"}, {"id": "cc81f3", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mi>R</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3fd"}, {"id": "16cc3a", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn><mi>R</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3fe"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e3ff", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ac"], "topics": ["60e2fb5766f9ce3f243b4f3c"], "concepts": ["60e40fd4f1ef260f84ed1e43"], "question": {"text": "Taking the wavelength of first Balmer line in hydrogen spectrum <math><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi></math> to <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></math> as <math><mn>660</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> , the wavelength of the <math><msup><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></mrow></msup></math> Balmer line <math><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi></math> to <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></math> will be :"}, "options": [{"id": "3383f9", "text": "<math><mn>889.2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e400"}, {"id": "13d082", "text": "<math><mn>488.9</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e401"}, {"id": "54afd3", "text": "<math><mn>388.9</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e402"}, {"id": "062f82", "text": "<math> <mrow>  <mn>642.7</mn><mtext>&#x2009;</mtext><mtext>nm</mtext></mrow></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e403"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e404", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ac"], "topics": ["6117b8be67dbe2603c3e8673"], "concepts": ["6162fb5a6ed13040ec84de56"], "question": {"text": "Choose the correct option from the following options given below :"}, "options": [{"id": "bc3eba", "text": "<p>In the ground state of Rutherford&#39;s model electrons are in stable equilibrium. While in Thomson&#39;s model electrons always experience a net-force.</p>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e405"}, {"id": "759002", "text": "<p>An atom has a nearly continuous mass distribution in a Rutherford&#39;s model but has a highly non-uniform mass distribution in Thomson&#39;s model</p>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e406"}, {"id": "c31aa4", "text": "A classical atom based on Rutherford&#39;s model is doomed to collapse.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e407"}, {"id": "c9d881", "text": "The positively charged part of the atom possesses most of the mass in Rutherford&#39;s model but not in Thomson&#39;s model.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e408"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e409", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ac"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4766"], "concepts": ["6117b98967dbe2603c3ea31d"], "question": {"text": "The time period of revolution of electron in its ground state orbit in a hydrogen atom is <math><mn>1.6</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>.</mo></math> The frequency of revolution of the electron in its first excited state (in <math><msup><mrow><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> ) is:"}, "options": [{"id": "f2d676", "text": "<math><mn>1.6</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>14</mn></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e40a"}, {"id": "bcda80", "text": "<math><mn>7.8</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>14</mn></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e40b"}, {"id": "88b789", "text": "<math><mn>6.2</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>15</mn></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e40c"}, {"id": "b5d126", "text": "<math><mn>5.6</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>12</mn></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e40d"}], "questionLabels": []}], "markingScheme": {"_id": "608283e223cf4b3ad8f125e6", "title": "JEE Single Correct", "correctAttempt": 4, "incorrectAttempt": -1, "createdAt": "2021-04-09T08:45:27.797Z", "updatedAt": "2021-07-05T05:39:15.785Z", "__v": 0, "updated_by": "6042252509c5bf34e8a2f178"}, "maximumAttemptLimit": 20, "linkedQuestions": [], "createdAt": "2026-04-14T14:28:47.521Z", "updatedAt": "2026-04-14T14:28:47.521Z", "__v": 0}, "position": 0, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e456"}, {"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e454", "title": "Physics Numerical", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e438", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ac"], "topics": ["6162fb5a6ed13040ec84de88"], "concepts": ["6162fb5a6ed13040ec84de5f"], "question": {"text": "<p>The mass defect in a particular reaction is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math>. The amount of energy liberated is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>7</mn></msup><mo> </mo><mi>kW</mi><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo></math> _____. (speed of light <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>8</mn></msup><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo> </mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>)</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "293c3e", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e439"}, {"id": "8c99e3", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e43a"}, {"id": "b42515", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e43b"}, {"id": "8f08b4", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e43c"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e43d", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ac"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4766"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b2d"], "question": {"text": "The radius of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>nd</mi></msup></math>&nbsp;orbit of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>He</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></math>&nbsp;of Bohr&#39;s model is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and that of fourth orbit of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Be</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;is represented as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;Now the ratio&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;The value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;is _____."}, "options": [{"id": "94f1a9", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e43e"}, {"id": "c2f533", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e43f"}, {"id": "fab06c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e440"}, {"id": "f31a67", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e441"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e442", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ac"], "topics": ["60e2fb5766f9ce3f243b4f3c"], "concepts": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52c0"], "question": {"text": "The first member of the Balmer series of hydrogen atom has a wavelength of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6561</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>&#8728;</mo></mover></math>. The wavelength of the second member of the Balmer series (in nm) is_____________"}, "options": [{"id": "d3a390", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e443"}, {"id": "7d9c27", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e444"}, {"id": "a7e873", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e445"}, {"id": "be0f72", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e446"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e447", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ac"], "topics": ["6117b8be67dbe2603c3e8673"], "concepts": ["6162fb5a6ed13040ec84de56"], "question": {"text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msqrt></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msqrt></math> are the impact parameters corresponding to scattering angles <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>60</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>90</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math> respectively, when an <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi></math> particle is approaching a gold nucleus. For <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>, the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> will be _____ ."}, "options": [{"id": "543a6f", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e448"}, {"id": "a966ff", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e449"}, {"id": "037ec1", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e44a"}, {"id": "ee07ca", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e44b"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e44c", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ac"], "topics": ["60e2fb5766f9ce3f243b4f3c"], "concepts": ["6117b5e3478ae845c43c5de3"], "question": {"text": "The first three spectral lines of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math>-atom in the Balmer series are given <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> considering the Bohr atomic model, the wave lengths of first and third spectral lines <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mfrac><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mfrac></mfenced></math> are related by a factor of approximately <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>,&nbsp;to the nearest integer, is ________."}, "options": [{"id": "016172", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e44d"}, {"id": "61fa25", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e44e"}, {"id": "953310", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e44f"}, {"id": "07aa49", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e450"}], "questionLabels": []}], "markingScheme": {"_id": "608283c623cf4b3ad8f125e5", "title": "JEE Numerical", "correctAttempt": 4, "incorrectAttempt": -1, "createdAt": "2021-04-09T08:45:27.797Z", "updatedAt": "2021-07-05T05:39:27.056Z", "__v": 0, "updated_by": "6042252509c5bf34e8a2f178"}, "maximumAttemptLimit": 5, "linkedQuestions": [], "createdAt": "2026-04-14T14:28:47.590Z", "updatedAt": "2026-04-14T14:28:47.590Z", "__v": 0}, "position": 1, "_id": "69de4f1f2ee0e063d923e457"}], "bonusSections": [], "packDetails": [], "paidFeatures": [], "tags": [], "timeRestrictionSlots": [], "createdAt": "2026-04-14T11:16:01.582Z", "updatedAt": "2026-04-17T04:58:01.374Z", "testType": "PYQs as Chapter Tests", "isResumeBufferAllowed": true, "enableAccessibility": true, "maxAttemptableQuestion": 2